{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1544472-vtr-rome-ways-of-the-senex","id":1544472,"title":"[VtR Rome] Ways of the Senex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-22T10:36:37-07:00","id":1544472,"title":"[VtR Rome] Ways of the Senex","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Requiem for Rome</b> questions - I\u2019m preparing story of Awakened mages fighting with Kindred vampires on control over mortals Senate of Republic Rome. ( Circa 220 BCE, just before Second Punic War ) I need some insight how vampires Camarilla and Senex influenced mortals government. Here are some opening questions I have.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">1. <b>When did Senex ( as Camarilla Wing ) was created?</b> When I look into <b>RfR</b> book, it says that circa 300 BCE is disappearance of Julius Senex. I do not see earlier creation date of Senex Wing. If it was destroyed \u2013 when it was rebuild?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">2. <b>HOW vampires of Senex influence mortal Senate?</b> Vampire are working only on nights, Senate works mostly on day times. Kindred of Rome have their Ghoul agents there? Are some Senators blood addicted from Kindred? How does it work?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">3. <b>What would be leaders of Senex circa 220 BCE, just before Second Punic War? </b>Maybe some Clan is very powerful then? I suspect Ventures are not now yet, only Julii Clan?</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T11:15:26-07:00","id":1544477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1544472-vtr-rome-ways-of-the-senex#post1544472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">2. <b>HOW vampires of Senex influence mortal Senate?</b> Vampire are working only on nights, Senate works mostly on day times. Kindred of Rome have their Ghoul agents there? Are some Senators blood addicted from Kindred? How does it work?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Dominate, vinculum and ghouls (human or animal, because Animalism). Also remember, many roman kindred, specially the Julii, will probably lean considerably on familial connections and the idea of them as venerable ancestors shades in flesh to influence and stay close to certain families.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1544472-vtr-rome-ways-of-the-senex#post1544472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">3. <b>What would be leaders of Senex circa 220 BCE, just before Second Punic War? </b>Maybe some Clan is very powerful then? I suspect Ventures are not now yet, only Julii Clan?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are no canon answers for this, any NPCs of the period will be 100% up to your imagination. Julii is THE clan in Rome with Vermes/Nosferatu right beside and below them. (As an aside, the Nosferatu Clanbook's version of the Vermes' origin tale cites something that sounds an awful lot like Zmai, the Worm, from the &quot;Horrors of an Ancient Age/Things That Should Not Have Been&quot; chapter of Predators, for Forsaken)<br /> <br /> Any kindred not of those clans would most likely be lone individuals and very small broods at most. Any way, they either are recognized &amp; somewhat accepted due to offering some important (religious/spiritual/supernatural) service to the Senex or foreign undead things that are seem as potential threats to be expelled or destroyed.<br /> Maybe vampires not of the Julii but somehow connected to one or more of the city-states in the Italian Peninsula could fit in a middle ground of sorts. Any clans possible, even &quot;apocryphal/lost&quot; ones depending on what wicked ideas cross one's mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-22-2024, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T13:35:45-07:00","id":1544493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1544472-vtr-rome-ways-of-the-senex?p=1544477#post1544477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any kindred not of those clans would most likely be lone individuals and very small broods at most. Any way, they either are recognized &amp; somewhat accepted due to offering some important (religious/spiritual/supernatural) service to the Senex or foreign undead things that are seem as potential threats to be expelled or destroyed.<br /> Maybe vampires not of the Julii but somehow connected to one or more of the city-states in the Italian Peninsula could fit in a middle ground of sorts. Any clans possible, even &quot;apocryphal/lost&quot; ones depending on what wicked ideas cross one's mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, I did read somewhere few months before in <b>RfR</b> - that <b>Daeva</b> were 'Greek slaves' Clan. So they would be in education and sex workers of this era, rather prominent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T14:19:00-07:00","id":1544500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1544472-vtr-rome-ways-of-the-senex?p=1544493#post1544493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, I did read somewhere few months before in <b>RfR</b> - that <b>Daeva</b> were 'Greek slaves' Clan. So they would be in education and sex workers of this era, rather prominent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, i did not remember that bit - if it is so, then there might be Daeva linked through these groups as an early form of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Camarilla_(VTR)?so=search#The_Peregrine_Collegia\" target=\"_blank\">Peregrine Collegia</a>, though other individuals connected to either foreign cults rising in popularity joining the Cult of Augurs are certainly possible, not to mention &quot;greek elders&quot; filling a role not unlike that on the Julii themselves among the still independent greek colonies present in the south and specially <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Sicily#Classical_Age\" target=\"_blank\">Sicily</a>.<br /> <br /> Also, i would suggest doing a good, long delve into the bloodlines, not only for extra color, but the bits of lore to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Galloi\" target=\"_blank\">compare</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gorgon_(VTR)\" target=\"_blank\">contrast</a> with the history of Rome as told by the Camarilla's not always reliable PoV. Without even going into the untold but quite significant hints of Strix touch one may get from the Gangrel clanbook - and possibly even more so from the 2e version of Protean.<br /> <br /> Plus, we have <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Akhud#Rome\" target=\"_blank\">those people</a>. Maybe. What they are or are not can be so very sketchy at times.... (Plus, so many cities ruined, razed or cursed through the ages - what is identified with Gomorrah in modern or late roman nights could have been an utterly different place - and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Veii#Conflict_with_Rome\" target=\"_blank\">much closer to home</a> - in a tale told before the rise to dominance of the Bible readers) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-22-2024, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T17:13:01-07:00","id":1544522,"title":"","content":"Anyway, if your chronicle is set circa 220 BCE, just before Second Punic War, that's about <b><i>580 years before</i></b> the time of the city as described in the &quot;Rome and the Necropolis&quot; chapter of Requiem for Rome, about a few decades before (or after?) the starting point of Fall of the Camarilla storyline.<br /> <br /> As distant from the nights of RfR as the rise of Dracula from modern nights of Requiem. Even in an era of not as fast-paced changes as our own, that's plenty room for some quite hefty divergence with things destroyed, created, lost or discovered. The Etruscans seemed so old and mysterious for the romans they had archeologists of sorts to study their stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1360391-seven-times-seven-is-still-seven\">This</a> old thread, for example, has some bits of pieces on VII that could be of interest either as alternate takes of it or wholy unrelated/independent bloodlines/covenants/shadow cults.<br /> <br /> Any bit of lore can be reskinned and twisted when you have almost 5-6 centuries of nebulous history between the extremes. And that without going into books written from a modern nights perspective - who's to say VII, Belial's Brood or whatever know their roots any better than the average L&amp;S or CoC neophyte?<br /> <br /> Damn, i remember there being a version of Zagreus for RfR that was considerably different from the one we are presented to in Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners.<br /> <br /> Anything from any book is fair game to a reboot toward your own preferences.<br /> <br /> And <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Eras\" target=\"_blank\">one more thing</a>, speaking of fodder to check, mine and adapt to your own tastes. Also, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ruins_of_Ur\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> terribly underated SaS (once adapted it <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuragic_civilization\" target=\"_blank\">N<b>UR</b>agic ruins</a> in WWII Sardinia, with some Pillar Men arc from JoJo inspiration in - but considering the Nuraghes were <i>already</i> millenium old ruins at the time of the Punic Wars, still quite valid fodder for your game, i dare say) and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Paterfamilias\" target=\"_blank\">another one</a> more directly related.<br /> <br /> Anyway, have a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QaNihFRvXaw\" target=\"_blank\">N<b>ur</b>aghe</a>-inspired visual or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A4Z_LnPxIPs&amp;list=PL9JZ-EBV7ILiXF3WXMygXrBuozDafbTAX&amp;index=2\" target=\"_blank\">two</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-23-2024, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T10:42:05-08:00","id":1545397,"title":"","content":"So I'm doing analysis of Clans of Kindred in Rome, circa 218 BCE ( Second Punic War ) - to populate my own Camarilla of that era, Senex especially.<br /> <br /> <b>Julii</b> - Most 'roman of Roman' vampires, siring from Remus founder of Rome<br /> <b>Daeva</b> - Exotic slaves and concubines, coming from Asia and Carthage<br /> <b>Nosferatu</b> - Original vampire of Etruscan ancient catacombs, first residents of caves making up Necropolis<br /> <b>Mekhet</b> - Those rare foreigners from Black Land of Egypt<br /> <b>Gangrel</b> - Those slaves coming with Gaul warriors ( Rome was already sacked by Gauls raiders in 387 BC, full on war with Gaul started with Punic Wars Era )<br /> <br /> My question is - <b>What Clan was vampire coming from Greece?<i> Daeva</i></b> maybe, as 'parts of Asia'?\ud83e\udd14 In 3rd century BCE most popular started to be educated by slaves from Greece in rich patrician households, Greeks becoming second ethnicity in city of Rome itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-05-2024, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}